body:
You'll not be able to mock the new object's persist method easily.

The only way I can see for this is to create a factory method inside your `Fruit` entity:

```
public static Fruit build() {
    return new Fruit();
}
```

Then mock this factory method to return a mock ...

@FroMage as doing `PanacheMock.doNothing().when(Fruit.class).persist();` will not work, we should generate a RuntimeException (checking the mocked method to be static from PanacheMock).
